WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.043 --> 00:00:18.272
We were imprisoned in the tunnel of ice. Ned banged the table with his fist.

2
00:00:18.274 --> 00:00:25.193
Conseil stayed quiet while I watched the captain. Once again Nemo's face betrayed no emotion.

3
00:00:25.194 --> 00:00:30.527
"Gentlemen," said Captain Nemo, "there are two ways of dying in this situation."

4
00:00:30.528 --> 00:00:35.931
He made these remarks as calmly as a mathematics professor lecturing his pupils would.

5
00:00:35.932 --> 00:00:41.439
"The first is to be crushed by the ice, and the second is to run out of air."

6
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:47.590
"We don't have to worry about running out of air, do we?" I asked. "Our reservoirs are full."

7
00:00:47.591 --> 00:00:53.256
"We have spent the last day underwater and already the submarine's air needs to be renewed.

8
00:00:53.257 --> 00:01:02.581
Obviously we can't get to the surface to refresh the air, and in two days—maybe three—we will have exhausted the supply in our reservoirs."

9
00:01:02.582 --> 00:01:07.408
"Well, Captain, can we get out of this situation by then?" I asked.

10
00:01:07.409 --> 00:01:14.035
"We will certainly try," he replied. "I'm going to run the Nautilus aground on the iceberg below us.

11
00:01:14.036 --> 00:01:18.732
My men will then put on their diving suits and attack the ice wherever it's the thinnest."

12
00:01:18.733 --> 00:01:23.653
Captain Nemo left the gallery, and the submarine soon began to sink slowly.

13
00:01:23.654 --> 00:01:31.732
"My friends," I said to Conseil and Ned, "we're in serious trouble here, but I rely on your courage and good spirits."

14
00:01:31.733 --> 00:01:40.367
"Professor," replied Ned, "I'm as handy with a pickax as I am with a harpoon, so if I can be useful to the captain, I'm willing to help him."

15
00:01:40.368 --> 00:01:44.375
"He won't refuse your aid," I said. "Come with me, Ned."

16
00:01:44.376 --> 00:01:49.621
I led him to the room where Captain Nemo and some crewmen were putting on their diving suits.

17
00:01:49.622 --> 00:01:53.684
I told the captain of Ned's offer, which the captain accepted.

18
00:01:53.685 --> 00:01:58.851
When Ned was dressed, I returned to the gallery and found Conseil looking out the windows.

19
00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:03.033
A few minutes later we saw a dozen men set foot on the ice.

20
00:02:03.034 --> 00:02:10.446
Captain Nemo drilled holes in the ice to determine where it was the thinnest, and then the men attacked the ice with their pickaxes.

21
00:02:10.447 --> 00:02:14.517
After two hours of hard work, Ned came in, exhausted.

22
00:02:14.518 --> 00:02:19.255
He and his comrades were replaced by new workers, including Conseil and me.

23
00:02:19.256 --> 00:02:25.509
The submarine's crew worked for twelve hours and managed to clear away only a small patch of ice.

24
00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:29.660
At this rate it would take us at least four days to get out of the tunnel.

25
00:02:29.661 --> 00:02:36.914
"And even if we do get out of this infernal prison," said Ned, "don't forget that we're still under the iceberg.

26
00:02:36.915 --> 00:02:41.677
Who knows how long it will be until we reach open water and can rise to the surface!"

27
00:02:41.678 --> 00:02:48.398
When I went out to work the next morning, it seemed as if the walls of the tunnel were starting to close in on us.

28
00:02:48.399 --> 00:02:53.485
I didn't say anything to Ned or Conseil, but I did mention it later to the captain.

29
00:02:53.486 --> 00:02:57.311
"I'm aware of that," he replied, as calm as ever.

30
00:02:57.312 --> 00:03:04.478
"It's one more danger, but the only thing to do is remove the ice faster than it is building up on the tunnel walls."

31
00:03:04.479 --> 00:03:08.636
I used my pickax even more vigorously the next time I went out.

32
00:03:08.637 --> 00:03:16.303
To tell the truth, it was a relief to work because the air in my diving suit was now so much better than the air onboard the Nautilus.

33
00:03:16.304 --> 00:03:24.208
But as soon as I stepped onto the ice the next day, I noticed that the side walls and the surface below us had visibly thickened with ice.

34
00:03:24.209 --> 00:03:27.962
The submarine would be crushed before we could free it!

35
00:03:27.963 --> 00:03:36.541
I was filled with despair and almost dropped my pickax. I found Captain Nemo and signaled to him that we needed to talk.

36
00:03:36.542 --> 00:03:40.866
We reentered the Nautilus, where we removed our diving suits.

37
00:03:40.867 --> 00:03:49.360
"We must take desperate steps, Professor Aronnax," said Captain Nemo, "or we will be sealed up in this ice as if in cement.

38
00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:54.191
If only my Nautilus were strong enough to bear this pressure without being crushed."

39
00:03:54.192 --> 00:03:58.445
"How much longer will the air last in the reservoirs?" I wanted to know.

40
00:03:58.446 --> 00:04:02.668
The captain looked me in the eye. "They will be empty tomorrow."

41
00:04:02.669 --> 00:04:09.605
Overcome with terror, I broke out into a cold sweat. Captain Nemo, meanwhile, appeared to be thinking hard.

42
00:04:09.606 --> 00:04:12.020
"Boiling water!" he muttered.

43
00:04:12.021 --> 00:04:14.351
"Boiling water?" I asked.

44
00:04:14.352 --> 00:04:18.274
"Yes, Professor Aronnax. We're in a relatively confined space.

45
00:04:18.275 --> 00:04:23.851
Wouldn't pumping boiling water into the sea raise its temperature enough to stop this ice from forming?"

46
00:04:23.852 --> 00:04:27.914
"I suppose so," I said. "Let's try it."

47
00:04:27.915 --> 00:04:32.740
Seawater was constantly being taken onboard and purified for drinking water.

48
00:04:32.741 --> 00:04:38.478
The captain now ordered the crew to heat this water to boiling and pump it back out into the sea.

49
00:04:38.479 --> 00:04:43.303
Slowly the temperature of the water surrounding the submarine began to rise.

50
00:04:43.304 --> 00:04:47.057
Five hours later the temperature had risen by two degrees.

51
00:04:47.058 --> 00:04:53.644
It continued to rise overnight until it was close to the freezing point—or melting point in this case.

52
00:04:53.645 --> 00:04:57.970
"We won't be crushed by the ice now," said Captain Nemo the next morning.

53
00:04:57.971 --> 00:05:02.382
"And we've made some real progress in removing the ice around the submarine."

54
00:05:02.383 --> 00:05:09.636
But now the reservoirs were out of air. As the day wore on, I felt as if a terrible weight were pressing on me.

55
00:05:09.637 --> 00:05:14.041
It was a relief when it was time to go outside and attack the ice.

56
00:05:14.042 --> 00:05:20.207
Back inside the submarine, I felt myself losing consciousness. Conseil took my hand.

57
00:05:20.208 --> 00:05:25.692
"If only I didn't have to breathe, I could leave more air for you," he told me.

58
00:05:25.693 --> 00:05:28.699
His unselfishness brought tears to my eyes.

59
00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:35.191
"Listen, Master," he said, cocking his head. "It sounds as if the water tanks are filling."

60
00:05:35.192 --> 00:05:39.762
He got up and looked out the windows. "And all the men have come inside."

61
00:05:39.763 --> 00:05:44.262
All of a sudden there was a cracking sound, and I knew what had happened.

62
00:05:44.263 --> 00:05:48.088
"We've broken through the ice below us," I whispered.

63
00:05:48.089 --> 00:05:51.659
"We're free!" Conseil shouted hoarsely.

64
00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:58.754
We had escaped from the tunnel, but how long would it be before we reached open water and could rise to the surface?

65
00:05:58.755 --> 00:06:06.000
After a while I no longer cared. Stretched out on a couch, I felt as if I were going to die.

66
00:06:06.001 --> 00:06:13.318
I could not see or hear or move a muscle, and I have no idea how many hours I spent like that.

67
00:06:13.319 --> 00:06:21.143
Suddenly I revived! Some breaths of air were filling my lungs. Had we risen to the surface of the ocean?

68
00:06:21.144 --> 00:06:26.993
No, Conseil and Ned, my two brave friends, were sacrificing themselves to save me.

69
00:06:26.994 --> 00:06:33.651
A little bit of air remained in the bottom of one breathing apparatus from a diving suit, and they were giving it to me.

70
00:06:33.652 --> 00:06:40.627
I wanted to push the air tank away, but they held it to my face, and for a few moments, I breathed freely.

71
00:06:40.628 --> 00:06:44.143
I looked at the clock and saw that it was eleven o'clock.

72
00:06:44.144 --> 00:06:49.453
Regaining some of my strength, I forced myself to get up and looked at the instruments.

73
00:06:49.454 --> 00:06:58.447
The Nautilus was twisting and turning through the water, moving at a rapid pace, and soon we were only twenty feet below the surface.

74
00:06:58.448 --> 00:07:02.217
But where was Captain Nemo? I wondered desperately.

75
00:07:02.218 --> 00:07:06.417
Were he and his crew even still alive?
